<title>USA: FSA qualifies 15 muni issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies 15 muni issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said Tuesday it qualified for bond insurance the following 15 municipal issues:</p>
<p>--Novato, Calif., $14.15 million refunding general obligations.</p>
<p>--Lawrence, Kan., $6.9 million water &amp; sewer revs.</p>
<p>--Boxborough, Mass., $7 million school GOs.</p>
<p>--Massachusettes $300 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Oakdale, Minn., $2.015 million tax increment GOs, $1.405 million refunding GOs and $4.105 million GO improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Hardyston Twp., N.J., $2.205 million GO improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Upper Moreland SD, Pa., $4.995 million GOs is a direct purchase.</p>
<p>--York County SD, S.C., $24 million school building bonds.</p>
<p>--Brownwood, Texas, $2.55 million street GOs.</p>
<p>--Meadows, Texas, $1.275 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Washington $28 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Muskego, Wis., $1.65 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
